    "body": "First of all, thank you for sharing this excellent work and for open-sourcing the project.\n\nI have successfully implemented the offline inference pipeline provided in the repository, and it works well. I am now exploring how to extend it into a real-time conversational avatar system.\n\nI have a question regarding the demo video. During the conversation, the avatar transitions into a \"listening\" state while the user is speaking, and then seamlessly starts speaking in between.\n\nCould you please clarify the following?\n\n1. How are the listening frames generated in real time? Are they generated online by the model?\n2. Since the avatar starts speaking in between while listening, how is the speech audio generated? What TTS system was used in the demo? Was it generated using an external streaming TTS, or was another approach used?\n3. Although the paper mentions that a real-time conversational avatar system can be built using the proposed acceleration techniques, the repository currently contains only the offline inference pipeline. Are there any plans to release the real-time streaming implementation or provide additional guidance on how the demo pipeline was built?\n\nIt would be great if I could get some guidance or assistance on implementing the real-time conversational pipeline. Any details, suggestions, or recommendations would be greatly appreciated.\n\nThank you again for your excellent work and for your time.",
