    "body": "Hi, thanks for releasing AvatarForcing.\n\nI'm observing significant identity drift during long-form generation. Depending on the reference image, the generated face starts degrading after roughly 30–60 seconds, eventually becoming noticeably distorted and losing resemblance to the source identity.\n\nThe issue appears to be highly dependent on the input face. Some identities remain stable while others drift consistently under the same settings.\n\nCould you please advise whether there are any recommended inference settings, preprocessing steps, or checkpoints to mitigate this issue? If this is a known limitation, are there any plans for a fix or improved checkpoint?\n\nInference Hardware : RTX 4090",
